    "text_rich_text_arGKcA": {
      "type": "text--rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "richtext_ncz3Jx": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The skin contains over 3 million sensory receptors that send signals to the central nervous system. The skin’s taste receptors — TRPV1 — respond to heat, acidity, and irritation. With chronic exposure, their activity increases, leading to discomfort, inflammation, and muscle tension.</p><p><strong>Re[Sens] technology reprograms TRPV1 through controlled stimulation using Sichuan pepper extract </strong>— a natural myorelaxant with botox-like action that reduces excessive nervous and muscular reactivity.</p><p>Studies show that<strong> just 15 minutes after application, muscle contractions decrease by 88%, helping to quickly relieve tension and reduce hypersensitivity.</strong></p>",
            "text_size": 16
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "richtext_ncz3Jx"
      ],
      "name": "t:sections.text--rich-text.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "background_color": "",
        "colors": "white",
        "section_width": "narrow",
        "text_alignment_desktop": "center",
        "text_alignment_mobile": "center"
      }
