    "text_rich_text_bKQy9m": {
      "type": "text--rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "richtext_eHtt93": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The CoNS flora plays a crucial role in maintaining the skin’s barrier function, regulating sebum secretion, and competitively suppressing pathogenic bacteria, particularly <em>Staphylococcus aureus</em>. With age and under stress, <strong>microbial balance deteriorates, reducing skin resistance and increasing sensitivity.</strong></p><p>Restoring balance with <em><strong>Lactobacillus casei</strong></em><strong> stimulates the expression of antimicrobial peptides, strengthens the barrier, and normalises sebum regulation — reducing inflammation and increasing the skin’s resistance to external aggressors.</strong></p>",
            "text_size": 16
          }
        }
      },
